Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:40:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Berrak: hold exit-routed loads until the httpx extension
 is installed

A link from another app can cold-start the browser before the bundled
extension has finished installing (reliably so on the first start after
an update). The interceptor then had no extension page to send the load
to and let it through, so with "Browse the web through the httpx exit"
on, that first page was fetched directly from the device. Seen on the
Pixel_10 emulator after upgrading the release build.

Such a load is now denied and held, the latest per session, and loaded
again once the install completes; if the install fails it stays held.
Loads the extension does not handle still go through untouched.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ec3g34YeceWefbDxePbgre
